  "sources": {
    "base": "rem Counting Capacitor Circuits\nrem https://projecteuler.net/problem=155\nrem Count the distinct capacitances of\nrem circuits of up to Count equal\nrem capacitors\n\nuse numbers\nuse sequences\nuse io\nuse cli\n\narg Count integer = 18\n\nrem A value p / q is stored as the key\nrem p K + q. Level m holds the circuits\nrem of m capacitors. Joining a level\nrem pair in parallel gives half of it,\nrem and the series joins are the\nrem reciprocals of those values.\nK = 8192\nStore = array 8193\nOff = array 0 0 1\nfor M in 2 to Count\n  Pairs = 0\n  for I in 1 to M // 2\n    Lo = Off (I + 1) - Off I\n    Hi = Off (M - I + 1) - Off (M - I)\n    Pairs += Lo * Hi\n  end\n  Out = array shape Pairs fill 0\n  Used = 0\n  for I in 1 to M // 2\n    J = M - I\n    for P in Off I to Off (I + 1) - 1\n      A = Store P // K\n      B = Store P mod K\n      for Q in Off J to Off (J + 1) - 1\n        C = Store Q // K\n        D = Store Q mod K\n        Num = A * D + B * C\n        Den = B * D\n        G = Num gcd Den\n        Key = Num // G * K + Den // G\n        Out Used = Key\n        Used += 1\n      end\n    end\n  end\n  Par = Out unique\n  Rec' = Par mod K * K + Par // K\n  Lev' = concat Par Rec unique\n  Store = concat Store Lev copy\n  End = array (Store len)\n  Off = concat Off End copy\nend\nAll' = Store unique\nAnswer = All len\nAnswer print\n",
    "rec": "rem Counting Capacitor Circuits\nrem https://projecteuler.net/problem=155\nrem Count the distinct capacitances of\nrem circuits of up to Count equal\nrem capacitors\n\nuse numbers\nuse sequences\nuse io\nuse cli\n\narg Count integer = 18\n\nrem A value p / q is stored as the key\nrem p K + q. Level m holds the circuits\nrem of m capacitors. Joining a level\nrem pair in parallel gives half of it,\nrem and the series joins are the\nrem reciprocals of those values.\nK = 8192\nStore = array 8193\nOff = array 0 0 1\nfor M in 2 to Count\n  Pairs = 0\n  for I in 1 to M // 2\n    Lo = Off (I + 1) - Off I\n    Hi = Off (M - I + 1) - Off (M - I)\n    Pairs += Lo * Hi\n  end\n  Out = array shape Pairs fill 0\n  Used = 0\n  for I in 1 to M // 2\n    J = M - I\n    for P in Off I to Off (I + 1) - 1\n      A = Store P // K\n      B = Store P mod K\n      for Q in Off J to Off (J + 1) - 1\n        C = Store Q // K\n        D = Store Q mod K\n        Num = A * D + B * C\n        Den = B * D\n        G = Num gcd Den\n        Key = Num // G * K + Den // G\n        Out Used = Key\n        Used += 1\n      end\n    end\n  end\n  Par = Out unique\n  Rec = Par mod K * K + Par // K\n  Lev' = concat Par Rec unique\n  Store = concat Store Lev copy\n  End = array (Store len)\n  Off = concat Off End copy\nend\nAll' = Store unique\nAnswer = All len\nAnswer print\n",
    "recsort": "rem Counting Capacitor Circuits\nrem https://projecteuler.net/problem=155\nrem Count the distinct capacitances of\nrem circuits of up to Count equal\nrem capacitors\n\nuse numbers\nuse sequences\nuse io\nuse cli\n\narg Count integer = 18\n\nrem A value p / q is stored as the key\nrem p K + q. Level m holds the circuits\nrem of m capacitors. Joining a level\nrem pair in parallel gives half of it,\nrem and the series joins are the\nrem reciprocals of those values.\nK = 8192\nStore = array 8193\nOff = array 0 0 1\nfor M in 2 to Count\n  Pairs = 0\n  for I in 1 to M // 2\n    Lo = Off (I + 1) - Off I\n    Hi = Off (M - I + 1) - Off (M - I)\n    Pairs += Lo * Hi\n  end\n  Out = array shape Pairs fill 0\n  Used = 0\n  for I in 1 to M // 2\n    J = M - I\n    for P in Off I to Off (I + 1) - 1\n      A = Store P // K\n      B = Store P mod K\n      for Q in Off J to Off (J + 1) - 1\n        C = Store Q // K\n        D = Store Q mod K\n        Num = A * D + B * C\n        Den = B * D\n        G = Num gcd Den\n        Key = Num // G * K + Den // G\n        Out Used = Key\n        Used += 1\n      end\n    end\n  end\n  Par = Out unique sort\n  Rec = Par mod K * K + Par // K\n  Lev' = concat Par Rec unique sort\n  Store = concat Store Lev copy\n  End = array (Store len)\n  Off = concat Off End copy\nend\nAll' = Store unique sort\nAnswer = All len\nAnswer print\n"
  },
